| editorial =
'''The basho and the bracket'''

The Nagoya Basho concluded today. Kotoyamada won his 8th championship. Asanoyama earned promotion to ozeki. The sport continues. The rankings update. The system works.

Tomorrow, the Emperor's Trophy bracket takes shape. 47 prefectural champions. The tournament is the largest high school sporting event in Okaiken. The Crown Prince will preside. The final is August 10. Between now and then, 47 schools will compete for the most prestigious trophy in Sanese high school sport.

The basho and the bracket. Both are systems. Both work. Both produce champions. The difference between a system that works and one that doesn't is not complexity. It is accountability.

